#%PAM-1.0
# Ryoku in-session lock — PASSWORD conversation
#
# Second of the lock screen's two parallel PAM conversations (see
# ryoku-lock for the fingerprint one). pam_fprintd's man page requires
# separate conversations for parallel methods. This service starts only after
# the secure lock proof is published for the foreground login1 session, then
# keeps a password prompt ready so typed input never waits out a scan.
#
# MODULE STACK:
#   auth  required    pam_unix.so nullok  <- typed password (empty allowed
#                                            only if the account has none)
#   account required  pam_unix.so         <- account validation
#   password required pam_deny.so         <- no password changes
#   session required  pam_unix.so         <- session setup

auth        required    pam_unix.so nullok
account     required    pam_unix.so
password    required    pam_deny.so
session     required    pam_unix.so
